aarch64 build of lsfg-vk 1.x: upstream https://github.com/PancakeTAS/lsfg-vk,
commit 62f8149 ("enhancement(flatpak): add support for 25.08", 2025-10-06),
the last commit before the 2.0 rewrite. Unmodified. Build it again with
scripts/build-lsfg-vk-arm64.sh (clang 18, Vulkan-Headers v1.4.321):
  cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
        -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++
  make -C build lsfg-vk
sha256 ec6e3a103b64c48e87af84cdb91b0cba46bd230dfed9b92c17caa8a5fb5db94a

Why 1.x and not 2.0: on Adreno (Turnip) lsfg-vk 2.0.0 and its master
(40d1e4e, 2026-10-06) draw garbage blocks in frame-generated games; 1.x does
not. FP16 is off (no_fp16 = true): with it, 1.x ran slower and stuttered.

decky-lsfg-vk 0.12.2 (PB-OS edition) writes ~/.config/lsfg-vk/conf.toml and
~/lsfg; games use the launch option `~/lsfg %command%`. The layer only acts in
a process whose name matches a [[game]] exe in that file (~/lsfg sets
LSFG_PROCESS=decky-lsfg-vk), so everything else runs untouched.

